diff --git a/plugin/agents/analyzer.md b/plugin/agents/analyzer.md
index f982939..01d31e0 100644
--- a/plugin/agents/analyzer.md
+++ b/plugin/agents/analyzer.md
@@ -900,10 +900,22 @@ design. If `mode == "code_review"`, go to §7 instead of transitioning to PLANNI
 ---
 
 ## 7. Review report (mode: code_review)
-Code review stops after a light situation analysis. Produce `review-report.md`
-(target, criteria, findings, recommendation), then `state-machine.transition` to the
-review_only terminal (same artifact the Orchestrator's review_only flow expects). No
-reproduction or fix plan.
+Code review uses the source-bound `structured-review` contract. Select an exact
+retained function identity and explicit go-local-review@1.0.0 pack, capture real
+CKS review_function and rule_candidates responses, and reuse the value/control
+analysis already included in the rule envelope. Never compute a parallel graph.
+Record six reasoning sections, original-node anchors, assumptions/unknowns,
+findings with priority/tradeoff, and review criteria. Unsupported/unavailable
+responses do not establish safety. The structural review lacks its own snapshot
+pin: its association is identity-only and must remain explicitly unverified.
+
+Build deep-review.json, deep-review-evidence.json, source-bound diagrams and a
+report draft with plugin/scripts/deep_review.py. Run the same verifier and bind
+states.ANALYSIS.deep_review_sha256 to exact artifact bytes before handoff. Follow
+review_only ANALYSIS -> PLANNING -> COMPLETION. The Planner validates the report
+and binds states.PLANNING.review_report_sha256. The delivery hook checks both;
+report delivery never grants independent human acceptance. No reproduction,
+production change, fix plan, tracker message or PR publication is implied.
 
 ---
 
